# What GitHub's language bar says this repo is.
#
# Linguist ignores prose by default, so it was measuring only the helper
# scripts and reporting the repo as Python. The product here is the Markdown:
# 79 files and roughly 1.3 MB of skills, prompt libraries and evals, against
# about 0.5 MB of Python and Shell that exist to serve them.
#
# So the one line below turns Markdown ON as a counted language. It does not
# turn anything off, and it does not relabel anything. The scripts are still
# first-party code we wrote and test in CI, so marking them vendored or
# generated would be a false claim about where they came from, and neither
# attribute is used here.
*.md linguist-detectable=true
